    {
      "id": "claim_46804935c6b54485beed63082df98895",
      "statement": "Two ArchUnit rules tighten Jackson usage: jacksonIsConfiguredGlobally permits only JsonHandling to create or configure a Jackson mapper (forbidding other classes from calling ObjectMapper/subclass constructors and the builder, shared, and rebuild methods), and noJackson2 forbids classes under edu.kit.kastel.mcse.ardoco.. from depending on com.fasterxml.jackson.core.. or com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.. while keeping the shared com.fasterxml.jackson.annotation package allowed. JsonHandling returns one shared immutable thread-safe Jackson 3 mapper built from JsonFactory.builderWithJackson2Defaults() with configureForJackson2() to preserve the Jackson-2-era serialized format, and offers an overload accepting custom StreamReadConstraints.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://core/framework/common/src/main/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/core/common/JsonHandling.java#L17-L58",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:195e7c954ee9227ab8becab001ca093ab2c0c5d7e4aa18c643a0ff162e5e1606:"
