    {
      "id": "claim_72d46298f41943da8914da683d5fccf5",
      "statement": "BasicArchitectureTest additionally enforces: configurableFieldsOnlyInConfigurableClasses (@Configurable fields only in AbstractConfigurable subclasses), traceLinksShouldBeFinal (every TraceLink subclass except TraceLink itself must be final), noForEachInCollectionsOrStream (forEach/forEachOrdered on Stream and List banned as side-effect lambdas), and preferEclipseCollections (interface methods outside ..metrics.. must not expose or accept raw JDK List/Set/SortedSet/Map/SortedMap types in favor of Eclipse Collections). A module-local TraceLinkArchitectureTest in core/framework/common's own test tree further requires non-private methods to use the base TraceLink type rather than its concrete subclasses in return and parameter positions.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://core/framework/common/src/test/java/edu/kit/kastel/mcse/ardoco/core/TraceLinkArchitectureTest.java#L17-L57",
